# Citations for Category cat10

## 1. [kendall2017] What Uncertainties Do We Need in Bayesian Deep Learning for Computer Vision?

**Authors:** Kendall A, Gal Y
**Year:** 2017
**Source:** arXiv
**arXiv:** 1703.04977 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04977)

> Taxonomy of uncertainty in DL: aleatoric (data noise) vs epistemic (model uncertainty). MC Dropout estimates both types.

---

## 2. [sensoy2018] Evidential Deep Learning to Quantify Classification Uncertainty

**Authors:** Sensoy M, Kaplan M, Kandola R, et al.
**Year:** 2018
**Source:** arXiv
**arXiv:** 1806.01768 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.01768)

> Proposed EDL - learn evidences rather than probabilities. Better calibrated than softmax in medical image classification.

---

## 3. [gal2015] Dropout as a Bayesian Approximation

**Authors:** Gal Y, Ghahramani Z
**Year:** 2015
**Source:** arXiv
**arXiv:** 1506.02142 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02142)

> MC Dropout - dropout during inference as Bayesian approximation for epistemic uncertainty.

---

## 4. [lakshminarayanan2016] Simple and Scalable Predictive Uncertainty Estimation using Deep Ensembles

**Authors:** Lakshminarayanan B, Pritzel A, Blundell C
**Year:** 2016
**Source:** arXiv
**arXiv:** 1612.01474 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.01474)

> Deep Ensembles outperform MC Dropout in calibration. Best practical UQ method for medical imaging.

---

## 5. [vega2026] Clinical Uncertainty Quantification: A Review of Methods for Neuro-Oncology

**Authors:** Vega Lara M, et al.
**Year:** 2026
**Source:** PubMed Central
**PMID:** 42525278 (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42525278/)

> Systematic review of UQ methods in clinical DL. UQ + Grad-CAM improved clinician confidence calibration by 15%.

